  "live_records": {
    "q-37517": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37517",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})-3{y}^{3}$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(\\sqrt{\\pi },2).$",
      "worked_solution": "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(\\sqrt{\\pi },2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})-3{y}^{3})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2})-3{y}^{3})\\,j \\\\  & =-2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2})\\,i-9{y}^{2}\\,j \\\\ ∇\\,f(\\sqrt{\\pi },2) & =-2\\sqrt{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡((\\sqrt{\\pi })^{2})i-9(2)^{2}\\,j \\\\  & =-2\\sqrt{\\pi }\\cdot 0\\,i-36\\,j \\\\  & =-36\\,j \\\\  & =⟨0,-36⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(\\sqrt{\\pi },2)\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨0,-36⟩\\cdot ⟨x-\\sqrt{\\pi },\\,y-2⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
